      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The 1842 Greek Revival Country Store has housed a general store on its main floor since opening, standing east of the common.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Petersham%2C_Massachusetts",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Petersham’s public library, founded in 1879, sits on the common in a brick building that hosts local history collections.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Petersham%2C_Massachusetts",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Expanding in 1938, the Quabbin Reservoir brought Petersham its largest land area, making it the largest town by area in Worcester County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
